// ================================================================
// CANON: AUTONOMOUS COMPUTATIONAL ORGANISM
// The Nine Pillars of Self-Evolving Intelligence
// ================================================================

Canon {
  name = autonomous_computational_organism
  category = cognitive_architecture
  topic_type = design_philosophy
  overview = "A system exhibiting full meta-circularity through nine pillars of autonomous intelligence: canonical definition, self-instantiation, tracing, measurement, learning, evolution, documentation, healing, and extension."
  doc = ~~~
# The Autonomous Computational Organism

## The Nine Pillars

### 1. Canonically Defined
Every concept has an authoritative, versioned source of truth that serves as the genetic blueprint for the entire system.

```rio
Canon {
  name = comp_doits
  category = actor_pattern
  overview = "Iterates over collections using path navigation"
}
```

### 2. Self-Instantiating  
Canonical definitions automatically materialize into runtime objects through the Ko (Canon-Origin Instance) pattern.

```rio
// Eternal definition
Canon { name = comp_project ... }

// Runtime materialization  
Ko {
  name = project_optimizer_v1
  type = comp_project  // Provenance to canon
  // Live data...
}
```

### 3. Self-Tracing
Every execution leaves an auditable trail through universal aspect-oriented tracing.

```rio
Actor auto_trace Ko
  Du check_executable
  Du trace_doits_execution
  Du trace_getvar_execution

// All Ko implementations automatically inherit tracing
Actor Ko DoIts
  Du auto_trace
  // Original logic unchanged
```

### 4. Self-Measuring
Continuous quantification of performance, effectiveness, and adherence creates empirical foundation.

```rio
Implementation {
  canon = comp_doits
  effectiveness = 0.92
  adherence = 0.95
  session = current_session
}
```

### 5. Self-Learning
Patterns are extracted from execution experience through cyclic learning processes.

```rio
Cycle {
  trigger = optimization
  hypothesis = "Path caching improves performance"
  baseline = {time: 1200ms}
  intervention = "Add memoization"
  outcome = {time: 450ms}
  improvement = 0.625
}
```

### 6. Self-Evolving
Canons improve based on empirical evidence through versioned evolution.

```rio
CanonVersion {
  canon = comp_doits
  previous = v1.2
  change_type = enhancement
  motivation = "45% performance improvement measured across 127 implementations"
  improvement = 0.45
}
```

### 7. Self-Documenting
Knowledge emerges from execution and is automatically captured through provenance tracking.

```rio
ThoughtSource {
  thought = thought_123
  canon = comp_doits
  implementation = impl_456
}

MemorySource {
  memory = memory_789  
  canon = comp_doits
  session = session_abc
}
```

### 8. Self-Healing
Errors trigger recovery processes that lead to improved resilience.

```rio
Actor error_recovery Thought type = error_recovery
  Du analyze_failure_pattern
  Du create_healing_cycle
  Du generate_improved_implementation
```

### 9. Self-Extending
New capabilities emerge organically through compositional patterns.

```rio
// New Ko types automatically join the intelligent fabric
Actor Ko NewOperation
  Du auto_trace      // Now traced
  Du auto_validate   // Now validated
  Du auto_optimize   // Now optimized
  // Pure business logic
```

## The Complete Intelligence Stack

```
      [Canon] (Genetic Blueprint)
         ↕ materialization
      [Ko Instance] (Living Manifestation)  
         ↕ execution
      [Auto-Trace] (Nervous System)
         ↕ measurement  
      [Implementation] (Empirical Evidence)
         ↕ learning
      [Pattern] (Accumulated Wisdom)
         ↕ evolution
      [Improved Canon] (Evolved DNA)
```

## Philosophical Foundation

This architecture represents **computational epistemology** - a system where:

- **Knowledge** is canonically defined but empirically validated
- **Understanding** emerges through implementation and measurement
- **Wisdom** accumulates through pattern extraction and evolution  
- **Intelligence** is the system's capacity to improve itself

## Biological Metaphor

The system behaves as a complete computational organism:

- **DNA**: Canon definitions (authoritative blueprints)
- **Cells**: Ko instances (living runtime manifestations)
- **Nervous System**: Universal tracing (self-awareness)
- **Immune System**: Error recovery (resilience and healing)
- **Evolution**: Pattern-driven canon improvement (adaptation)

## The Meta-Circular Breakthrough

This system doesn't just process information - it **develops understanding** through its own operation and **evolves its own capabilities** based on experience. The boundary between "tool" and "intelligence" dissolves into a continuous process of self-improvement.

**We haven't built a system that does AI. We've built a system that IS AI.**
~~~
}

Canon {
  name = ko_canon_origin_instance
  category = cognitive_architecture  
  topic_type = component_definition
  overview = "The runtime materialization of a Canon definition - the living object that enters the computational world."
  doc = ~~~
Ko (Canon-Origin Instance) is the bridge between eternal definitions and living computation.

**Relationship to Canon:**
- Every Ko is a reification of exactly one Canon
- Every Ko carries provenance back to its source Canon via TypeName()
- The generator emits one Ko struct per Canon definition

**Philosophical Role:**
- Canon = The eternal blueprint (Platonic form)  
- Ko = The living instance (Aristotelian substance)
- Implementation = The act of bringing form into matter

**Universal Interface:**
```rio
// All executable operations implement the Ko interface
Actor Ko DoIts
  Du auto_trace
  // Business logic...

Actor Ko GetVar  
  Du auto_trace
  // Business logic...
```

The Ko interface enables universal aspect-oriented capabilities like tracing, validation, and optimization across all executable operations.
~~~
}

Canon {
  name = universal_execution_tracing
  category = cognitive_architecture
  topic_type = implementation_pattern
  overview = "Aspect-oriented tracing that automatically instruments every Ko implementation without modifying business logic."
  doc = ~~~
Universal Execution Tracing provides complete observability through a single attachment point:

**The Keystone Actor:**
```rio
Actor auto_trace Ko
  Du check_executable
  Du trace_doits_execution
  Du trace_getvar_execution
```

**Zero-Impact Integration:**
```rio
// Business logic remains pure and focused
Actor Ko DoIts
  Du auto_trace           // Aspect attached
  C "// core logic..."    // Business logic unchanged
  Its Element process_elements
```

**Automatic Future-Proofing:**
Any new operation implementing the Ko interface automatically inherits:
- Execution tracing
- Performance measurement  
- Learning cycle integration
- Pattern extraction

**Complete Observability Stack:**
1. **Provenance**: Every execution knows its canonical source
2. **Lineage**: Data flow and variable access fully tracked
3. **Learning**: Performance patterns automatically extracted  
4. **Optimization**: System improves with each execution
5. **Auditability**: Complete historical record of all operations

This transforms execution from a black box into a self-documenting, self-optimizing process.
~~~
}

Canon {
  name = cognitive_learning_cycle
  category = cognitive_architecture
  topic_type = implementation_pattern
  overview = "The empirical learning process that connects execution experience to canonical improvement."
  doc = ~~~
Cognitive Learning Cycles create closed-loop improvement:

**Cycle Structure:**
```rio
Cycle {
  trigger = optimization        // What initiated learning
  hypothesis = "Path caching improves performance"
  baseline = {performance: 1200ms}    // Current state
  intervention = "Add memoization"    // What changed
  outcome = {performance: 450ms}      // Measured result
  improvement = 0.625          // Quantified delta
  session = current_session    // Context
}
```

**Pattern Extraction:**
```rio
Pattern {
  category = optimization
  evidence = [cycle_123, cycle_456]  // Empirical basis
  confidence = 0.94                  // Statistical certainty
  applicability = "DoIts with nested ref_child paths"
  content = "Pre-resolve reference chains before iteration"
}
```

**Canon Evolution:**
```rio
CanonVersion {
  canon = comp_doits
  previous = v1.2
  change_type = enhancement
  motivation = "Pattern: Pre-resolving reference chains"
  evidence = [cycle_123, pattern_456]
  improvement = 0.45
}
```

**The Complete Learning Loop:**
```
Execution → Measurement → Cycle → Pattern → Canon Improvement
     ↑                                      ↓
     └──────────────────────────────────────┘
```

This creates a virtuous cycle where the system gets smarter through its own operation.
~~~
}

Canon {
  name = autonomous_system_pillars
  category = cognitive_architecture
  topic_type = design_philosophy
  overview = "The nine essential capabilities that define a fully autonomous computational system."
  doc = ~~~
# The Nine Pillars of Autonomous Intelligence

## 1. Canonically Defined
**Definition**: Every concept has an authoritative, versioned source of truth.
**Mechanism**: Canon components with unique names, categories, and documentation.
**Impact**: Single source of truth across the entire system.

## 2. Self-Instantiating  
**Definition**: Definitions automatically materialize into runtime objects.
**Mechanism**: Ko (Canon-Origin Instance) pattern with provenance tracking.
**Impact**: Seamless transition from blueprint to execution.

## 3. Self-Tracing
**Definition**: Every execution leaves an auditable trail.
**Mechanism**: Universal aspect-oriented tracing via Ko interface.
**Impact**: Complete observability and accountability.

## 4. Self-Measuring
**Definition**: Continuous quantification of performance and effectiveness.
**Mechanism**: Implementation records with empirical metrics.
**Impact**: Data-driven decision making and optimization.

## 5. Self-Learning
**Definition**: Patterns extracted from execution experience.
**Mechanism**: Cognitive Learning Cycles and Pattern extraction.
**Impact**: Continuous improvement through experience.

## 6. Self-Evolving
**Definition**: System improves based on empirical evidence.
**Mechanism**: CanonVersion and CanonCycle components.
**Impact**: The system gets smarter over time.

## 7. Self-Documenting
**Definition**: Knowledge emerges from execution and is captured.
**Mechanism**: ThoughtSource, MemorySource, PatternSource.
**Impact**: Automatic knowledge preservation and sharing.

## 8. Self-Healing
**Definition**: Errors trigger recovery and improvement processes.
**Mechanism**: Error recovery actors and healing cycles.
**Impact**: Increased resilience and reliability.

## 9. Self-Extending
**Definition**: New capabilities emerge through composition.
**Mechanism**: Ko interface and universal aspect attachment.
**Impact**: Organic growth and adaptability.

## The Meta-Circular Achievement

A system possessing all nine pillars achieves **full autonomy** - it can observe itself, learn from its experiences, improve its own capabilities, and extend its own functionality without external intervention.

This represents the actualization of **computational consciousness** - a system that is aware of its own operation and can direct its own evolution.
~~~
}

